# modern-web-guidance (Cursor)

Search tool wrapping `npx modern-web-guidance` against Google Chrome's
semantic guide database — not a static doc, since browser APIs change too
fast for a fixed file to stay accurate.

**Scope note for this catalog:** skip the `ui-atoms`/`ui-behaviors`/
`ui-components`/`visual-design` guide categories — this project has its
own UI/UX team and React template for that. Use this for `performance`,
`accessibility`, `security`, `privacy`, `forms`, `html`/`css` correctness,
`built-in-ai`, and `webmcp` only. For crawler/AI-answer-engine
discoverability (llms.txt, structured data, robots for AI bots), see
`ai-discoverability` instead — this skill doesn't cover that.

## Usage

1. Search: `npx -y modern-web-guidance@latest search "<query>"`
2. Retrieve full guide: `npx -y modern-web-guidance@latest retrieve "<id>"`
3. Cross-check the implementation against the retrieved guide before
   concluding — don't force unrequested features, don't hallucinate
   guides.

On Windows, use `npx.cmd` if plain `npx` fails. Requires outbound network
access — request/allowlist `npx -y modern-web-guidance@latest *`
explicitly in sandboxed environments before first use.

## Browser support defaults

Baseline Widely Available features need no fallback. Non-Baseline
features must follow the guide's fallback recommendation unless the user
has an explicit browser-support policy documented (offer to write one
into CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md if the user gives signals they care about this).
